1
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:51,440
Who is Chen Xiaofang?

2
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:55,480
That's me.

3
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,280
Zhou Fang said you're very bossy.

4
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:00,360
Zhou Fang?

5
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,640
What's your relationship with him?

6
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:07,480
We're very closely related.

7
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:10,040
He has to call me Cousin Great-Grandaunt.

8
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,320
Great-Grandaunt?

9
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,480
And a cousin, at that?

10
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:15,880
Forgive my bluntness,

11
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:17,880
I haven't met many living great-grandaunts.

12
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,560
That's how big families are.

13
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:20,720
There are many branches.

14
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,240
You're just ignorant.

15
00:02:25,960 --> 00:02:27,080
Miss Cousin Great-Grandaunt,

16
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,480
right this way, please.

17
00:02:28,480 --> 00:02:29,160
Have a seat first.

18
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,880
This is our Duoduo.

19
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:47,200
I want to hold a grand funeral for him.

20
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:50,040
A crystal coffin.

21
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:51,120
A mountain of flowers.

22
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,720
A 24-person professional mourning team.

23
00:02:54,320 --> 00:02:56,520
The urn must be a limited edition.

24
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:58,960
Pick a grave with excellent feng shui.

25
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:03,640
Feng shui?

26
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:06,440
A pet funeral?

27
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:06,960
That's impossible.

28
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:07,840
You must be joking.

29
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,360
I'm sorry,

30
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,560
Miss Cousin Great-Grandaunt.

31
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,880
You made this trip for nothing.

32
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:14,160
Our shop only handles funerals for people.

33
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,240
He was with me for over ten years.

34
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,920
How is he not family?

35
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:27,640
What a pity.

36
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,000
I prepared this 200,000 for nothing.

37
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:31,400
This 200,000...

38
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:32,720
Can't be spent here after all.

39
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:36,120
Please forgive the offense,

40
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:37,240
Miss Cousin Great-Grandaunt.

41
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:39,880
Please, take a seat.

42
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,160
Bro, go pour some water!

43
00:03:42,160 --> 00:03:44,560
Let me explain our services to you in detail.

44
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,280
After all, dogs are man's best friend.

45
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:48,240
Your feelings are completely understandable.

46
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:50,800
Our Duoduo loves pink.

47
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:52,760
Even a dazzling pink works.

48
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:55,680
I want a gold-plated paper house.

49
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:56,600
Gold-plated and diamond-studded...

50
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:57,400
We can make that happen.

51
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:03,400
Do you think I'm dead?!

52
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:08,200
Our ancestors taught us to bury humans,

53
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,560
not to mourn an animal!

54
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:14,480
You're ruining our old shop's reputation!

55
00:04:17,520 --> 00:04:20,280
If I'm ruining it, I'm using my money!

56
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:22,280
This little bit of money

57
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:25,360
won't ruin Xiaoxitian's reputation!

58
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:29,680
Is this enough?

59
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:34,720
As the saying goes, hang a dead cat on a tree,

60
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,480
and throw a dead dog in the river.

61
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:42,280
This is the rule left by our ancestors.

62
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:44,480
A funeral for a beast?

63
00:04:44,960 --> 00:04:47,400
No amount of money will make it happen!

64
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:53,680
Oh, Dad!

65
00:04:54,680 --> 00:04:57,760
I saw many animals age and die at the zoo.

66
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:00,560
In the end, they're no different from us.

67
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,760
Don't you always talk about respecting life?

68
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,840
A human's life is a life,

69
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:05,800
but isn't a dog's life a life too?

70
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,200
Aren't animal lives still lives?

71
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:07,960
Exactly!

72
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,600
Dad, you're being such a hypocrite.

73
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:10,840
Old man,

74
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,240
you might be an old fossil,

75
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,800
but your son and daughter are quite sensible.

76
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,600
Are you going to take this job or not?

77
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:21,280
It doesn't matter to me.

78
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,880
I can spend my money anywhere.

79
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:26,240
But I must hold a funeral for Duoduo.

80
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:29,600
The people my great-grandson Zhou Fang picked

81
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:30,640
must be the right choice.

82
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:34,520
Leaving Duoduo to you,

83
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:35,200
I feel completely at ease.

84
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:38,080
I'll leave the money with you for now.

85
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,080
Old man,

86
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:45,680
you should learn from your son.

87
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,200
Keep up with the times.

88
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,600
Take care, Miss Cousin Great-Grandaunt!

89
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:53,600
Take your money back!

90
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,440
Dad, forget it.

91
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:54,840
No, no, no!

92
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:55,800
I...

93
00:05:56,920 --> 00:06:00,480
If any of you takes this funeral job today,

94
00:06:02,680 --> 00:06:04,760
I'll disown you!

95
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,760
It's 200,000!

96
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:18,880
Brother Jianguo,

97
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,160
"Who says creatures' lives don't matter?

98
00:06:24,360 --> 00:06:26,080
They have the same flesh and skin as us."

99
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,040
Animals...

100
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:31,120
How can they be compared to humans?

101
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,200
Here you go.

102
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,440
Here.

103
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:46,400
Thanks, Uncle Daren.

104
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:47,640
No problem.

105
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:49,560
Uncle Daren's treating today.

106
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,400
Uncle Daren.

107
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,600
I've got a lot of money now.

108
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,400
Just let me splurge a bit.

109
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:55,880
Alright.

110
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:57,760
The beers will be on me, alright?

111
00:06:58,400 --> 00:06:59,200
Deal.

112
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,160
I'll have ten chicken hearts.

113
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,040
You got it.

114
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,640
Order whatever you like.

115
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:03,280
Alrighty.

116
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,200
Thanks, Uncle Daren.

117
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,360
Today,

118
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,600
with this first glass,

119
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,160
I want to toast my dear brother.

120
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:14,960
If it weren't for your impassioned speech,

121
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:16,880
this deal would've probably fallen through.

122
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,600
Chen Baixi,

123
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,720
Rich ladies really have a thing for you.

124
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:28,800
You know what,

125
00:07:28,960 --> 00:07:31,600
She might've chased him here from Beijing.

126
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,760
So tell me, along the way,

127
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,600
how many girls has he messed around with?

128
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,960
You two sure can make up stories.

129
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:40,840
Actually,

130
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,560
Besides out-of-towners, there's a local.

131
00:07:44,440 --> 00:07:45,240
Who?

132
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:47,280
Fan Shiqi.

133
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:52,760
Miss Fan.

134
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,480
Right, right.

135
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:54,120
There's her too.

136
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,320
Li Yiran,

137
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:02,960
you care so much about me,

138
00:08:02,960 --> 00:08:04,480
could it be that you're jealous?

139
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:20,280
Are you two secretly dating behind my back?

140
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,960
No way.

141
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:24,640
I'm not a rich woman.

142
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:25,680
Your brother wouldn't go for me.

143
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,080
You're right.

144
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,640
Anyway, for today's order,

145
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,960
I'm definitely taking it.

146
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,520
The principle of putting money first...

147
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:40,480
You've stuck with it since we were kids.

148
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:43,640
Actually, in first-tier cities,

149
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,760
Pet funerals have been a thing for years.

150
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:47,240
It's not exactly new.

151
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:50,760
But spending 200,000 for a pup's funeral...

152
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,040
This is definitely a first.

153
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,000
In a small place like Lecang,

154
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:56,600
with Great-Grandma Qimeng paying so much,

155
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,120
everyone must be fighting over it.

156
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,600
Dad was right about one thing.

157
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:05,400
If word gets out we did a dog's funeral,

158
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,560
who would trust you with their elders?

159
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:08,880
I was thinking...

160
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:09,440
Tell me.

161
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,360
What if we use Great-Grandma's order

162
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:13,800
to try

163
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,360
and see if we can get pet funerals going?

164
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:18,080
Didn't you tell us during the training?

165
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,720
Someone has to be the first to take the leap.

166
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:21,600
Right.

167
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,160
We have to be pioneers.

168
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:26,400
Xiaofang, let me tell you,

169
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,320
I've sorted everything out with my dad.

170
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:29,080
Come on, cheers.

171
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,400
Oh, really?

172
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:31,640
Then call your dad right now.

173
00:09:31,640 --> 00:09:32,600
I'll confront him.

174
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,080
Honey,

175
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,280
you're living your life with me,

176
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:43,560
not with my dad.

177
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,560
Why do you always care about what he thinks?

178
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,600
Do you have any idea

179
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:52,000
that your Cousin Great-Grandaunt came?

180
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:53,680
Of course I do.

181
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:56,440
I begged for it in the family group chat.

182
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:57,920
I wanted to contribute

183
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,360
to my wife's career.

184
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,720
Zhou Fang, are you crazy?

185
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:04,680
I...

186
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,720
How am I crazy?

187
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:07,800
Brother-in-law,

188
00:10:07,800 --> 00:10:08,920
what did I do wrong this time?

189
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:11,760
Zhou Fang,

190
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:15,520
sometimes doing nothing is a big mistake.

191
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,320
So what do I do now?

192
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,160
Go after her!

193
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,640
Xiaofang!

194
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:26,040
Xiaofang!

195
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:40,400
You scared the hell out of me.

196
00:10:40,800 --> 00:10:42,480
I thought someone was trying to rob me.

197
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,080
Who'd steal your book?

198
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,400
You fall asleep the second you read.

199
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:46,400
You fall asleep the second you read.

200
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:47,320
When are you gonna change?

201
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,360
This is very complicated.

202
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,880
Did you know?

203
00:10:58,520 --> 00:11:00,240
You went out for barbecue, didn't you?

204
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,680
And you didn't even bring any back for me.

205
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:04,440
You can smell that?

206
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:07,320
We got a huge 200,000 order today.

207
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,360
Xiaofang treated us.

208
00:11:09,480 --> 00:11:10,320
200,000?

209
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,360
Who is so generous?

210
00:11:15,040 --> 00:11:16,320
Do they need a professional mourner?

211
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:18,080
My market rate is 800.

212
00:11:18,120 --> 00:11:19,240
I'll give you 400.

213
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:20,240
But you have to quote them 800.

214
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,680
You keep 400 as a kickback.

215
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:22,720
Are you serious?

216
00:11:23,040 --> 00:11:23,840
Absolutely.

217
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:24,800
Deal.

218
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,240
Well, it's not a person.

219
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,000
It's a dog.

220
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,440
That won't work.

221
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,440
If I mourn for a dog,

222
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,520
what am I supposed to call it?

223
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:34,520
No, no way.

224
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:35,600
A dog is just too ridiculous.

225
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,520
I wouldn't be able to cry.

226
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:38,480
What's wrong?

227
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,080
Do you also think

228
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:42,200
a funeral for a dog is inappropriate?

229
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:50,240
A funeral for a dog...

230
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,120
In principle,

231
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:54,440
there's nothing inappropriate about it.

232
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:57,520
A dog is a life too.

233
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:59,000
They have parents too, after all.

234
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,720
Right?

235
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,080
When they arrive,

236
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:03,760
every life deserves a proper welcome.

237
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:05,560
When they leave,

238
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,400
every life deserves a proper farewell.

239
00:12:09,080 --> 00:12:10,400
I just can't help but think how

240
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:12,760
a rich family's dog

241
00:12:13,440 --> 00:12:15,360
is worth more than a poor person's life.

242
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:17,760
Don't you think?

243
00:12:17,760 --> 00:12:19,200
Lan!

244
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,040
Come down and play mahjong!

245
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,920
Coming, coming!

246
00:12:23,920 --> 00:12:24,920
Give me a second.

247
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:25,880
I'll be right down!

248
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:27,640
Take my glasses back inside.

249
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:09,440
Ancestors.

250
00:13:09,440 --> 00:13:13,480
I, Chen Jianguo, failed to raise my kids.

251
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:18,880
That's why they're so rebellious.

252
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:27,880
Dad.

253
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:29,640
What is it?

254
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,200
Take a few steps to the door.

255
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:34,280
Stand there.

256
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,280
Open your mouth.

257
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,760
Did you taste anything?

258
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:39,840
Taste what?

259
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,760
Nothing but cold air.

260
00:13:42,720 --> 00:13:44,400
With the current economy,

261
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,840
running a business is insanely competitive.

262
00:13:45,840 --> 00:13:48,560
How many of our jobs actually make money?

263
00:13:49,280 --> 00:13:50,200
Times have changed.

264
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:52,040
The industry needs to transition.

265
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:53,920
And our mindset needs to change too.

266
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:57,200
Our ancestors' rules can't be broken.

267
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,080
Dad, why are you coughing?

268
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:04,880
None of your business.

269
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:08,680
You must face the consequences yourself.

270
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:09,840
Uncle Chen.

271
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:10,760
Calm down, calm down.

272
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:16,080
About this pet funeral business,

273
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:18,040
I looked up some data last night.

274
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:20,400
I found out the scale of the pet economy

275
00:14:20,400 --> 00:14:22,040
has already exceeded 400 billion.

276
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:24,240
And there are 100 million pet owners.

277
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:28,480
Three million pets pass away every year.

278
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:30,960
Based on data from smaller cities,

279
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:33,240
the pet funeral penetration rate is 3.6%.

280
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,160
Dad,

281
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,680
we have to keep up with the times.

282
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,400
What's a penetration rate?

283
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:41,760
Quick, explain it.

284
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:45,840
Simply put, out of every 100 pet owners,

285
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,840
